[I] A bootloader and experimentation playground for Apple Silicon

[T] m1n1 is the bootloader of Asahi Linux for Apple Silicon Macs, which
[T] bridges the Apple boot flow and loads U-Boot or a Linux kernel with a
[T] device tree. It also serves as a hardware experimentation playground,
[T] which can be driven from Python over USB for reverse engineering.

[U] https://github.com/AsahiLinux/m1n1

[A] Asahi Linux Project
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] base/boot
[F] CROSS NO-LTO
[R] + arm64

[L] MIT
[V] 2.0.1

[D] 77aaf8099f09ea04579b2b3af90960dfc48b6c209ece445e1d29b468 m1n1-2.0.1.tar.gz https://github.com/AsahiLinux/m1n1/archive/v2.0.1/

var_append makeopt ' ' AS=$CC
var_append makeopt ' ' OBJCOPY=$OBJCOPY

# build core/alloc from rust-src for aarch64-unknown-none-softfloat
var_append makeopt ' ' BUILDSTD=1
var_remove GCC_WRAPPER_REMOVE ' ' '-march*'
makeinstopt=
hook_add postmake 5 "install build/m1n1.{macho,bin} $root/boot/"
